# Linux kernel config fragment: Bluetooth (onboard UART + USB) and USB audio.
#
# Filename is historical (started Bluetooth-only); it now also carries the
# USB-audio class driver. Applies to every target — the RPi onboard-BT symbols
# below are inert on non-RPi targets (e.g. x86_64) but harmless.
#
# CANONICAL COPY. Edit here, then run `make sync` to materialize identical
# copies into each target subdir (rpi3/, rpi4/, ...). The per-target copy is
# what the build references (subdir-local path keeps git `sparse:` consumption
# and artifact checksums correct).
#
# Merged over each target's base defconfig via
# BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES. `make olddefconfig` (run by the
# Nerves kernel build) only pulls in symbols reached via `select`, NOT via
# `depends on` — a dependent symbol whose `depends on` prerequisite is unmet
# is silently dropped. So list every `depends on` prerequisite explicitly.
# CONFIG_RFKILL is already in the stock rpi3 base defconfig.
#
# SERIAL_DEV_BUS (+ the ttyport controller) is the serdev core that
# BT_HCIUART_SERDEV `depends on`. Without it the kernel never binds the
# `bluetooth` serdev node under the UART, so no hci0 auto-attaches at boot.
# (Verified on rpi3 hardware: v0.1.0 set BT_HCIUART_SERDEV=y but, lacking
# SERIAL_DEV_BUS, olddefconfig reverted it to n and /sys/bus/serial was absent.)
CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_BUS=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_DEV_CTRL_TTYPORT=y
CONFIG_BT=y
# hci_uart is a MODULE on purpose. Built in (=y), its serdev probe races the
# squashfs root mount and can request the BCM .hcd patch before /lib/firmware
# exists (seen on rpi3: "BCM: firmware Patch file not found" logged 1 ms
# before "VFS: Mounted root"; chip init then times out — Opcode 0x1003 /
# 0x0c14 -110 — and hci0 stays dead for the whole boot). As a module it loads
# via the OF-modalias uevent after the rootfs is up — modules and firmware
# ship on the same filesystem — so the patch lookup can't race the mount
# (same path brcmfmac already relies on). The sub-options below are bools
# compiled into the hci_uart module, so they stay =y.
CONFIG_BT_HCIUART=m
CONFIG_BT_HCIUART_SERDEV=y
CONFIG_BT_HCIUART_BCM=y

# USB Bluetooth adapters (btusb). Separate driver/path from the onboard
# UART chip: btusb auto-probes on USB enumeration (no serdev/attach), so a
# dongle just appears as a new hciN. CONFIG_USB is already on in the base
# defconfig. The chip sub-options below are `default y` under BT_HCIBTUSB,
# but listed explicitly per the select-vs-depends-on note above. NOTE:
# firmware-bearing dongles (Realtek rtl_bt, MediaTek, Intel) still need
# their blobs in /lib/firmware (linux-firmware) — not provided here;
# firmware-free (CSR-style) dongles work with just the driver.
CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB=y
CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB_BCM=y
CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB_RTL=y
CONFIG_BT_HCIBTUSB_MTK=y

# USB audio class driver — USB DACs (playback) and USB ADCs (capture). The one
# snd-usb-audio driver is bidirectional, so this covers both; class-compliant
# devices need no per-vendor driver. The base defconfig has SND=m and the SoC
# cards as modules, but a *builtin* USB-audio driver can't depend on a modular
# core, so promote the SND core (and the deps SND_USB_AUDIO selects:
# PCM/RawMIDI/HWDEP) to =y. Building =y (not =m) guarantees the driver is
# resident on hotplug rather than relying on USB module autoload — same choice
# as btusb above. SND_USB is the menu gate (depends on USB, already =y);
# SND_USB_AUDIO depends on it. CONFIG_SOUND is already =y in the base defconfig.
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_PCM=y
CONFIG_SND_HWDEP=y
CONFIG_SND_RAWMIDI=y
CONFIG_SND_USB=y
CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO=y

# USB mass storage (SMB backup share source). USB_STORAGE `depends on` USB
# && SCSI, and BLK_DEV_SD `depends on` SCSI (SCSI itself `depends on` BLOCK,
# already default y) — per the select-vs-depends-on note above, none of
# these are pulled in automatically by olddefconfig, so all three are listed
# explicitly. USB (the host stack) is =y in six base defconfigs but ABSENT
# on rpi0/rpi0_2 (gadget-mode boards): they set CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y but not
# CONFIG_USB, so USB_STORAGE's `depends on USB` was silently dropped by
# olddefconfig — verified in their built kernel .configs. It's listed
# explicitly here per the select-vs-depends-on rule. On those two boards the
# host stack is inert without a host-mode controller but keeps all 8 kernels
# uniform. Six of the eight targets already carry these three =y in their
# base defconfigs; this fragment makes rpi0/rpi0_2 (gadget-mode boards with
# no practical USB host storage — build-only uniformity) and x86_64 (today
# SCSI is only implied via virtio) uniform with the rest.
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_SCSI=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_SD=y
CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y

# exFAT + NTFS3 filesystems, for mounting whatever filesystem a backup drive
# already has (the app pushes a one-click ext4 reformat instead of fixing up
# in place — neither exFAT nor NTFS get a journal from us). In 6.18 both
# EXFAT_FS and NTFS3_FS `select` NLS, BUFFER_HEAD and LEGACY_DIRECT_IO
# (verified against v6.18 fs/exfat/Kconfig + fs/ntfs3/Kconfig), so unlike
# the USB storage chain above, no `depends on` prerequisites need listing
# here. NLS_UTF8 is already =y in all 8 base defconfigs (needed for the
# iocharset=utf8 mount option below). NTFS3_FS_POSIX_ACL is deliberately
# left off.
CONFIG_EXFAT_FS=y
CONFIG_EXFAT_DEFAULT_IOCHARSET="utf8"
CONFIG_NTFS3_FS=y
CONFIG_NTFS3_LZX_XPRESS=y
